# A whole SQL query after a pipe gets the same rewrite help as at the start of a query.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | SELECT a FROM t
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..25
  PIPELINE@0..24
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    ERROR@9..24
      IDENT@9..15 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
      IDENT@16..17 "a"
      WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
      IDENT@18..22 "FROM"
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      IDENT@23..24 "t"
  WHITESPACE@24..25 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `SELECT ... FROM` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:10
  |
1 | from t | SELECT a FROM t
  |          ^^^^^^   ---- in DataScript the table comes first
  |          |
  |          this is SQL
  |
  = help: start with the table and pipe it into operators: `from t | project a`
